t' activity must occur at least once in the process.\",\"template\":\"Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity involves formally documenting a security incident with its severity and type.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":1},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' must not occur in the process.\",\"template\":\"Absence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Emergency Drill\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' activity involves running a simulated emergency drill for security staff. This activity is strictly forbidden in the process.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":1},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"Exactly one of the activities 'Train Security Staff' or 'Conduct Emergency Drill' must occur in the process instance. This means that the process is compliant if only 'Train Security Staff' occurs without any occurrence of 'Conduct Emergency Drill', or only 'Conduct Emergency Drill' occurs without any occurrence of 'Train Security Staff'. The process is non-compliant if both 'Train Security Staff' and 'Conduct Emergency Drill' occur, or if neither occurs. The constraint enforces a mutual exclusivity and a mandatory occurrence of one of the specified activities.\",\"template\":\"Exclusive Choice\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Train Security Staff\",\"description\":\"The 'Train Security Staff' activity involves providing training to security personnel on protocols and procedures.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Emergency Drill\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' activity involves running a simulated emergency drill for security staff. This activity is strictly forbidden in the process.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If an 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity occurs, then a 'Review Security Footage' activity must eventually occur after the 'Inspect Security Cameras' event at some point in the same process instance. The response must occur for the same Camera ID. There is no requirement on how soon or what events may occur in between. Multiple 'Inspect Security Cameras' can be pending at the same time, and a single 'Review Security Footage' can fulfill the obligation for all preceding 'Inspect Security Cameras'. If 'Inspect Security Cameras' does not occur, the constraint imposes no obligation on the occurrence of 'Review Security Footage'.\",\"template\":\"Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Inspect Security Cameras\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity involves examining security camera feeds for potential security issues.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Review Security Footage\",\"description\":\"The 'Review Security Footage' activity involves reviewing recorded security camera footage for evidence or investigation purposes.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Camera ID == T.Camera ID\",\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"Whenever an 'Alert Security Personnel' activity occurs, it must be immediately followed by an 'Escort Suspect' activity in the next event position, with no other events in between. This constraint is only active if the alert occurs at a High Security Level, and the suspect must be escorted by the same Personnel ID that was alerted. This must occur within a time frame of 0 to 5 minutes.\",\"template\":\"Chain Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Alert Security Personnel\",\"description\":\"The 'Alert Security Personnel' activity involves notifying security staff of a potential security threat or incident.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Escort Suspect\",\"description\":\"The 'Escort Suspect' activity involves physically 