es addressing and resolving customer complaints related to security procedures.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Customer ID == T.Customer ID\",\"time_condition\":\"0,1,h\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Escort Suspect' activity is permitted to occur only if a 'Report Incident' activity has occurred before it within the same process instance. This constraint is only active if the Incident Type is Theft.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Escort Suspect\",\"description\":\"The 'Escort Suspect' activity involves physically escorting a suspected individual out of the store or to a designated area.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity involves formally documenting a security incident with its severity and type.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"T.Incident Type is Theft\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If 'Perform Security Audit' activity occurs, then 'Update Security Protocols' must also occur in the same process instance, and vice versa. This constraint is only active if the Audit Score is less than 50, meaning both activities must be executed when the audit score is below 50.\",\"template\":\"Co-Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Perform Security Audit\",\"description\":\"The 'Perform Security Audit' activity involves conducting a comprehensive security audit and assigning a score.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Update Security Protocols\",\"description\":\"The 'Update Security Protocols' activity involves revising and updating the store's security protocols based on audit findings.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Audit Score < 50\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' activity cannot be immediately followed by a 'Report Incident' activity; there must be at least one other event between them. Similarly, a 'Report Incident' event cannot be immediately preceded by a 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' event. This constraint allows multiple occurrences of 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' and 'Report Incident' in any order, provided they are not adjacent in the event sequence.\",\"template\":\"Not Chain Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Check Inventory Discrepancies\",\"description\":\"The 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' activity involves reviewing inventory records for discrepancies that may indicate theft or loss.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity involves formally documenting a security incident with its severity and type.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Deactivate Alarm' activity cannot be preceded by a 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity within the same process instance. This means that if any 'Verify Alarm Trigger' event has occurred before a 'Deactivate Alarm' event in the process instance, then 'Deactivate Alarm' is disallowed. All instances of 'Deactivate Alarm' must occur before any instance of 'Verify Alarm Trigger'.\",\"template\":\"Not Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Deactivate Alarm\",\"description\":\"The 'Deactivate Alarm' activity represents the terminal phase of the process where the security alarm is deactivated.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Verify Alarm Trigger\",\"description\":\"The 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity involves confirming whether an alarm has been legitimately triggered.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If a 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity occurs with a status of Resolved for a given Customer ID, then a 'Conduct Bag Check' activity for the same Customer ID must not occur an